    "title": "UConn's Dan Hurley mingles with Michigan's 'Fab Five'",
    "text": "UConn head coach Dan Hurley speaks during a press conference as the Huskies prepare for the NCAA National Championship Game against Michigan at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis, Ind., Sunday, April 5, 2026.Dave Zajac/Hearst Connecticut MediaYou never know who you might encounter in the middle of a live television interview.UConn men's basketball coach Dan Hurley was in the midst of an interview with Matt Norlander from CBS Sports Saturday night following the Huskies' victory over Illinois in the national semifinals when the fabled members of Michigan's \"Fab Five\" walked past.Article continues below this adGet Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.ONLY 25¢That included Juwan Howard, himself a former Michigan head coach, and Chris Webber, who gave Hurley a hug. Michigan won the other Final Four game against Arizona, setting up Monday's national championship game.The other members of the Fab Five were Jalen Rose, Jimmy King and Ray JacksonThe Fab Five went to consecutive national championship games themselves in 1992 and 1993, losing to Duke and North Carolina, respectively. Hurley's older brother, Bobby, played for Duke in that 1992 final, clinching the Blue Devils' back-to-back national championships.Article continues below this adDan Hurley said he attended a Nike Camp and played in the Dapper Dan Roundball Classic, which used to held in Pittsburgh, with members of the Fab Five. This was back when Hurley played for his father at St. Anthony's in New Jersey before he went to play for Seton Hall.\"The thing when you're a player, it was still a thrill,\" Hurley said. I hadn't seen a number of them in person in a number of years, except Juwan. But seeing Jimmy King and Jalen and C Webb and then ... yeah, that was a pretty cool moment. At first, it's like, Fab Five, as they were walking by me. That was pretty cool. Then Juwan, we made eye contact, and about Tarris (Reed, who played for Howard at Michigan), he's like, 'I'm happy for him.' \"Article continues below this adScore exclusive insights and analysis on UConn athletics.April 6, 2026Joe Morelli is a high school sports reporter with GameTimeCT. He coversr boys basketball, girls soccer and golf of all ages throughout the state, among other sports. He joined the New Haven Register in 1997 and has been with GametimeCT since its inception..",
